The legal texts are laws of the Republic of the Congo, taken from the Journal officiel de la
République du Congo as published by the Secrétariat général du Gouvernement (https://sgg.cg),
retrieved 29-30 October 2026.

Laws, court decisions and decisions of administrative authorities are outside the scope of
copyright in the Republic of the Congo. Loi n° 24-82 du 7 juillet 1982 sur le droit d'auteur et les
droits voisins, art. 14: "Nonobstant les dispositions des articles 6 et 7 ci-dessus, les lois, les
décisions de justice, celles des autorités administratives, ainsi que la traduction officielle de ces
textes et les nouvelles du jour publiées, radiodiffusées ou communiquées au public, sont hors du
champ d'application de la présente loi."
The site sgg.cg states no reuse terms that restrict this, and its robots.txt allows automated access.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text of each act was read from the Journal officiel PDF, its two
columns joined into paragraphs, hyphenated line breaks rejoined, and each version converted to one
Markdown file per article, with one paragraph per line, and arranged as git commits dated on the day
the change took effect. The wording of the law was not changed. The Secrétariat général du
Gouvernement does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

Further sources (from 2026-11-27):
- FAOLEX, the FAO legal database (https://faolex.fao.org/): records and PDFs reused under FAO's terms
  (non-commercial reuse with acknowledgement: "Source: FAOLEX, FAO"); the texts are official Congolese
  texts, outside copyright under art. 14 above.
- Ministère de l'Économie, documentation library (economie.gouv.cg, no longer answering): copies kept
  by the Internet Archive Wayback Machine (https://web.archive.org/), official texts.
- Cour constitutionnelle de la République du Congo (https://cour-constitutionnelle.cg): official
  texts; the site states "Tous droits réservés", which cannot attach to texts excluded by art. 14.
- WIPO Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/): official texts, free access.
- Ministère des Finances (https://www.finances.gouv.cg/fr/documentation), and the ministry sites
  hydrocarbures.gouv.cg, primature.gouv.cg, sante.gouv.cg and gouvernement.cg: official texts published
  for the public; no reuse restriction stated.
- assemblee-nationale.cg (in maintenance, files answer HTTP 500), budget.gouv.cg (down) and
  commerce.gouv.cg (rebuilt, files gone): official texts, copies kept by the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.
- Commission de la CEMAC (https://cemac.int): community acts (règlements, directives, actes
  additionnels), official texts published for the public; no reuse restriction stated.
- Not used: beac.int (its legal notice forbids rediffusion of its content).
- Not used: sgg.cg. Its legal notice (https://sgg.cg/fr/mentions-legales.html) forbids any reproduction
  of the site or its content without prior express authorisation of the Secrétariat général du
  Gouvernement; texts already taken from it on 28-30 October 2026 (the Constitution, Loi n° 29-2019,
  Loi constitutionnelle n° 2-2022) stay, and nothing further is taken from it.
